<title>SPAIN: Spain's Helguera seeks layoffs of 240 employees.</title>
<headline>Spain's Helguera seeks layoffs of 240 employees.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish express freight firm Helguera Uniexpress has petitioned the Labour Ministry to lay off 240 employees, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The official, who asked not to be named, told Reuters the company has had an excess of workers since it merged in 1996 with TNT Uniexpress.</p>
<p>The General Workers Union (UGT), one of Spain's leading trade unions, is fighting the layoffs, a representative said.</p>
<p>&quot;This (layoff) is being negotiated because they are losing money,&quot; UGT representative Francisco Garrido said. &quot;The problem is the company is expanding and buying other companies while laying off experienced workers.&quot;</p>
<p>Helguera has about 930 employees.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585-8341</p>
